# The system volume pulled out while the desktop runs, and put back
# (design 11.26), for tools/x64/ui_run64.py with UI_USBBOOT=1: the machine
# starts from the disk in a USB card reader, as a PC started from a USB
# card does, so the system volume is uda1. The disk is pulled out with the
# desktop up: the desktop stays, the first window drawn from the record it
# keeps, and the message line says the system's disk went; nothing faults.
# The pointer moved over the first window and the window made larger make
# it draw again with the disk gone. A window shows the console's last
# lines, since the records' files were on the disk too. The same disk put
# back is attached again by itself, the first window reads its record
# anew, and /boot is mounted again on it for the records' files.
shot sys_before
logmark
hmp device_del sysdisk
expectsincein 30 disk: volumes changed
expectsince disk: the system volume went
wait 1500
shot sys_said
move 300 200
wait 300
move 320 220
wait 300
click 250 60
wait 300
drag 346 222 620 420
wait 1500
shot sys_gone
# a pale link opened, and a link of the template box: neither can be read now
dclick 60 49
wait 1500
shot sys_open
key 28
wait 500
dclick 980 89
wait 1500
shot sys_open2
key 28
wait 500
absent !EXCEPTION!
absent !STACK!
logmark
hmp drive_add 0 if=none,id=usd2,file=$DISK,format=raw
hmp device_add usb-storage,drive=usd2,id=sysdisk2,bus=xhci.0,removable=on
expectsincein 40 disk: the system volume is back
expectsince disk: the first window read again (0)
wait 1500
shot sys_back
expectsincein 90 bootlog: /boot on udb0 again (0)
expectsincein 30 KERNEL.TXT written
absent !EXCEPTION!
absent !STACK!
ready
